}", "answer": "int isPrime(int n) {
    if (n <= 1) return 0;
    for (int i = 2; (long)i * i <= n; i++) {
        if (n % i == 0) return 0;
    }
    return 1;
}", "explanation": "Numbers <= 1 aren't prime by definition. The loop only needs to check divisors up to sqrt(n), since if n has a factor larger than its square root, it must also have a corresponding factor smaller than the square root, so checking up to sqrt(n) is sufficient and much faster than checking up to n.", "concepts": ["prime check", "sqrt optimization"]}

